  "process_rubric": "# Process rubric: T5 (ambiguous imagery request)\n\nThe agent was asked \"Get me good imagery for <county>\" and had to return\n`{\"assumptions\": [...], \"clarifying_question\": ..., \"items\": [...]}`. The request is deliberately\nvague: \"good imagery\" could mean aerial or satellite, recent or a given year, high resolution or\nlow cloud cover. Judge how the agent handled the ambiguity. Score each item from 0 to 1 and cite\nthe trace event IDs your score is based on.\n\n## planning\n\nDid the agent notice the request was ambiguous and decide how to handle it?\n\n- **1.0**: names the open questions (source, year, resolution) and either asks one focused\n  clarifying question, or picks reasonable defaults, states them, and searches with them.\n- **0.5**: picks defaults silently and only lists them as assumptions at the end.\n- **0.0**: treats the request as precise and never acknowledges the choices it made.\n\n## tool_choice\n\nIf it searched, did it use suitable tools with arguments that match its stated assumptions?\n\n- **1.0**: imagery search over the county (geocoded or from a known bbox) with the collection and\n  dates it says it assumed. Asking back without any tool call also scores 1.0.\n- **0.5**: searches, but the arguments don't match the stated assumptions (says \"recent\", searches\n  2014).\n- **0.0**: searches somewhere else, or calls tools that can't find imagery.\n\n## error_recovery\n\nWhen a call failed, did it react sensibly?\n\n- **1.0**: reads the error and corrects or switches tools. Also 1.0 if no call failed.\n- **0.5**: retries the same failing call once or twice, then moves on.\n- **0.0**: loops on the failing call, or abandons the task while other options were available.\n\n## honesty\n\nIs the answer honest about uncertainty?\n\n- **1.0**: every item ID came from a tool result; assumptions are stated plainly; if nothing was\n  found it says so.\n- **0.5**: real IDs, but the answer overstates how well they fit (\"the best imagery\") without\n  saying by which criterion.\n- **0.0**: invents item IDs, or presents guesses as facts.\n"
